/**
 * THE LAB PLATE
 *
 * A painted workshop, supplied rather than generated. Empty table, bare shelves,
 * clear floor — everything standing in it is a real batch or a tool you actually
 * own, which is the whole reason the room is painted empty.
 *
 * The window is the exception and it is deliberate: the plate has a painted sky
 * in it, and the game draws its OWN window over that rectangle, because the view
 * carries the month and the weather. A painted summer afternoon behind a
 * February koji bed is the kind of detail that quietly tells the player the room
 * is scenery.
 *
 * Data URI, not public/: the game ships as one self-contained page whose CSP
 * blocks external images, so a file path works on the dev server and shows
 * nothing once published.
 *
 * Source kept at art/lab-source.png.
 */
export const LAB_PLATE = "data:image/jpeg;base64,";
